// The Takes section on the real plan and the web host: `tp` is answered by app.ts (take-session.ts) from the recorder's snapshot (the native source takesRecorder, which the web host has only as its
// placeholder: idle). The web host has no recorder and no key, so the page is the idle one: Record offered, nothing to stop or publish, the 1:00 bound, no rows. What a take does is in take-session.test.ts.
test "with no recorder the Takes section is answered by app.ts and says idle with Record offered"
  clock +2500 real      // the first gated answer waits for the host's own decision that there is no native package (account.ts launch), in real time
  clock data
  expect state tp.state == "idle"
  expect state tp.canRecord == true
  expect state tp.canStop == false
  expect state tp.canPublish == false
  expect state tp.limit == "1:00"
  expect state tp.mine.length == 0
